WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:14.871
The fever still had a strong grip on Beth, but like a little soldier, she fought it every

2
00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:15.592
step of the way.

3
00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:19.755
Meg and Jo tirelessly rotated shifts to care for Beth.

4
00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:25.460
Hannah also helped hugely by looking after all the household chores that the girls couldn't do.

5
00:00:26.656 --> 00:00:31.719
During Beth's illness, Meg and Jo discovered many things about their sister that they hadn't known before.

6
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.502
For example, who would have known that shy little Beth had so many friends?

7
00:00:38.543 --> 00:00:43.005
When word got out that she was sick, every day someone would come by with a gift or

8
00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:43.826
flowers for her.

9
00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:50.269
The living room rapidly filled with beautiful blooms and lovely presents that Jo knew Beth would cherish.

10
00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:52.410
"How kind.

11
00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:56.676
Everyone is thinking of our Beth," remarked Meg, folding some washcloths.

12
00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:02.718
Her eyes followed Jo as she carried to the table several loaves of fresh bread, courtesy of the

13
00:01:02.758 --> 00:01:05.599
baker, who had just come by to ask about Beth.

14
00:01:06.319 --> 00:01:11.400
Jo, hands perched on her hips, stared at the large amount of food that neighbors and friends had

15
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:11.941
brought over.

16
00:01:11.961 --> 00:01:17.182
"Meg, if you were Beth, what do you think you would do with all this food?"

17
00:01:17.522 --> 00:01:20.043
asked Jo, pointing to the overflowing table.

18
00:01:20.943 --> 00:01:26.554
Meg, catching on to Jo's line of thinking, replied, "I think I would share whatever I had."

19
00:01:27.675 --> 00:01:33.679
Jo smiled at her sister, whom she was grateful to have during these painful times, and said, "Yes,

20
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:34.280
I agree.

21
00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.342
That is exactly what she would do."

22
00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:42.747
Meg and Jo generously filled a large basket with the food that had been kindly given to Beth.

23
00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:48.251
"I hope the Hummel children aren't too sick to enjoy this," said Jo as she placed the loaves

24
00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:49.512
of fresh bread in the basket.

25
00:01:50.384 --> 00:01:55.508
"Dr. Bangs said that the Hummel children didn't catch the fever as severely as our Beth," said Meg.

26
00:01:55.528 --> 00:02:00.711
"That may mean our Beth will recover soon, too," Jo said hopefully.

27
00:02:01.652 --> 00:02:06.895
Nodding but without commenting on her sister's last remark, Meg said, "We should have done this sooner.

28
00:02:07.556 --> 00:02:10.197
I must confess all this to Mother when she returns."

29
00:02:11.138 --> 00:02:13.019
"I wonder if we should send for Mother now?"

30
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.421
asked Jo as she pulled on her coat.

31
00:02:16.682 --> 00:02:17.242
"I don't know.

32
00:02:17.883 --> 00:02:22.465
I just wish she were here right now," replied Meg, wrapping a scarf around her neck.

33
00:02:23.465 --> 00:02:29.046
Clutching one handle each, the sisters carried the basket between them to divide the weight, but nobody could

34
00:02:29.106 --> 00:02:31.187
share the heavy burden of guilt on their hearts.

35
00:02:32.587 --> 00:02:35.488
The visit to the Hummels wasn't as horrible as Jo expected.

36
00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:41.190
Mrs. Hummel was still distressed over the death of her little baby, and although the girls tried to

37
00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.610
console her, she was too upset to be comforted.

38
00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:49.752
The other children, thinner from their illness, were extremely excited when they saw the large basket of goodies.

39
00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:55.299
After spending a fair amount of time with them, Meg and Jo returned home with lighter hands and

40
00:02:55.339 --> 00:03:00.683
hearts. Meg went upstairs to check up on Beth, giving Jo some time to spend alone.

41
00:03:01.724 --> 00:03:05.066
Jo went outside, hoping the cold air would clear her head.

42
00:03:05.086 --> 00:03:08.509
"Jo? What are you doing out here?"

43
00:03:09.149 --> 00:03:13.992
Laurie had seen his friend sitting alone on a large rock in the yard and decided to join

44
00:03:14.032 --> 00:03:18.856
her. "I just needed some fresh air," said Jo, putting on a brave face.

45
00:03:19.828 --> 00:03:20.688
"How are you coping?"

46
00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:21.689
Laurie asked.

47
00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:24.510
"Okay," said Jo meekly.

48
00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:30.332
"No need to lie to me, friend," said Laurie, tilting Jo's head upward to face him.

49
00:03:30.352 --> 00:03:36.035
"You're right, I'm not doing fine," said Jo before she burst into tears.

50
00:03:36.055 --> 00:03:40.216
"If Beth dies, I will never forgive myself."

51
00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:43.218
"Stop talking nonsense.

52
00:03:43.938 --> 00:03:48.660
Dr. Bangs thinks Beth will recover soon; it's just a matter of time.

53
00:03:49.516 --> 00:03:54.440
I know what will transform that frown into a smile," said Laurie, getting up and dusting off his

54
00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.584
bottom. "Laurie, I don't feel like laughing," Jo said wearily.

55
00:04:00.465 --> 00:04:04.408
"Nonsense! Someone once told me that laughter is the best medicine.

56
00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:05.689
Now watch this."

57
00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:12.495
Laurie began to imitate his grandfather, then Hannah, Brookes, and finally each of the girls.

58
00:04:13.595 --> 00:04:15.917
Jo had to guess which person he was mimicking.

59
00:04:16.858 --> 00:04:21.417
Before she knew it, she was laughing happily, forgetting her troubles for just a moment.

60
00:04:21.437 --> 00:04:23.979
"I just wish Mother were here.

61
00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:28.221
She would know what to do," said Jo after Laurie had finished his performance.

62
00:04:29.341 --> 00:04:34.404
Laurie playfully pulled Jo's short hair and said, "What if I told you that she's coming home, as

63
00:04:34.444 --> 00:04:34.984
we speak?"

64
00:04:36.005 --> 00:04:40.147
Stunned, Jo looked at him hopefully and said, "Mother is coming home?

65
00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.409
How? When?"

66
00:04:42.429 --> 00:04:45.070
"Dr. Bangs told me to send for her.

67
00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.532
I didn't want to tell you girls in case it worried you more.

68
00:04:49.544 --> 00:04:51.545
She should arrive here tonight," said Laurie.

69
00:04:52.545 --> 00:04:58.967
Jo burst into tears again, sobbing loudly and hiccupping as she said, "Thank you, Laurie.

70
00:04:59.107 --> 00:04:59.807
Thank you."

71
00:05:00.587 --> 00:05:04.069
Hugging his friend, Laurie sat with Jo until her tears stopped.

72
00:05:04.849 --> 00:05:08.970
Jo did not tell Meg about Mother's arrival, for fear her sister might think the worst.

73
00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.411
"I wonder how Father is doing?"

74
00:05:11.651 --> 00:05:12.251
whispered Meg.

75
00:05:12.271 --> 00:05:14.712
"We haven't had a letter in two days."

76
00:05:15.768 --> 00:05:20.090
"Mother mentioned that he had such an appetite that he wanted to eat up her portion of their

77
00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.651
meals," Jo said smiling, as she recalled Mother's last letter.

78
00:05:23.671 --> 00:05:25.352
"Oh, that's right.

79
00:05:25.752 --> 00:05:28.233
He's even started to walk a little," said Meg.

80
00:05:28.253 --> 00:05:30.074
"I never read that part.

81
00:05:30.414 --> 00:05:31.095
How do you know?"

82
00:05:31.475 --> 00:05:32.575
Jo asked, surprised.

83
00:05:33.316 --> 00:05:37.577
Meg turned red and lowered her eyes before answering, "John said so."

84
00:05:37.597 --> 00:05:40.118
"John? Who is John?"

85
00:05:40.359 --> 00:05:41.599
Jo asked rather loudly.

86
00:05:41.619 --> 00:05:44.080
"Mr. Brookes.

87
00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:48.102
His name is John Brookes," Meg said in a dreamy voice.

88
00:05:49.303 --> 00:05:56.327
Jo was beyond words because, with everything that had happened recently, she had forgotten about Laurie's secret.

89
00:05:57.487 --> 00:06:00.669
Now it seemed as if the cat was out of the bag.

90
00:06:00.689 --> 00:06:04.231
"Meg, have you been writing to Mr.

91
00:06:04.351 --> 00:06:07.033
Brookes? That's very unladylike!"

92
00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:10.995
Jo scolded, borrowing Amy's favorite descriptive word for her.

93
00:06:11.015 --> 00:06:13.308
"Don't worry, Jo.

94
00:06:13.328 --> 00:06:15.789
I only wrote a few times to thank him for his help.

95
00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:20.871
Besides, there is nothing improper about our writing," Meg said firmly.

96
00:06:21.712 --> 00:06:28.175
Before Jo could speak her mind, the door suddenly opened and a familiar figure walked in, paralyzing the

97
00:06:28.215 --> 00:06:30.736
girls for a moment before they realized who it was.

98
00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:35.638
"Mother!" Meg and Jo screamed together as they ran to hug her.

99
00:06:35.658 --> 00:06:41.048
"We're so happy you've returned," said Jo.

100
00:06:41.068 --> 00:06:43.670
"Thank you, girls," Mother replied, kissing them.

101
00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:49.073
Then she knelt down beside Beth and said, "Don't worry, love, Mother is here."

102
00:06:50.014 --> 00:06:55.378
Meg and Jo confessed their wrongdoings to Mother, preparing to be disciplined for their selfishness.

103
00:06:56.378 --> 00:07:01.001
Instead, Mother just said to them, "Seeing your sister suffer like this is punishment enough.

104
00:07:01.662 --> 00:07:04.084
I hope you girls have learned a lesson from all this."

105
00:07:04.844 --> 00:07:08.887
Then Mother took them in her arms and hugged them and told them to continue praying for Beth.

106
00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:13.822
The next day, Jo immediately noticed a change in Beth's breathing.

107
00:07:14.742 --> 00:07:16.203
It was slower and more relaxed.

108
00:07:17.504 --> 00:07:20.445
The rash seemed to have faded and Beth looked more peaceful.

109
00:07:21.426 --> 00:07:24.728
"The fever has broken," Mother said in a trembling voice.

110
00:07:25.808 --> 00:07:30.191
Jo ran over and held Mother's outstretched hand, asking, "Is she going to live?

111
00:07:30.551 --> 00:07:31.672
Will Beth be all right?"

112
00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:38.616
With tears of relief streaming down her face, Mother replied, "Yes, our little girl is going to make

113
00:07:38.636 --> 00:07:38.716
it."
